# Data roots are never committed. `data/` is a symlink to bulk storage; the
# intermediate RA/Dec extracts alone are ~14 GB and are fully regenerable from
# the plate scans, so they are outputs, not sources.
#
# Two exceptions, both small, both derived entirely from public headers, and
# both load-bearing. The CRPIX table (55 KB): without it a third of plates carry
# a ~2.3" systematic and nothing errors out. The plate manifest (5 KB): it is the
# footprint definition, and both README and REPRODUCING tell users to pass it.
# Excluding the directory outright meant git never descended into it, so
# `/data/*` is required for these negations to work -- a bare `!` under a
# directory exclusion is silently useless.
/data/*
!/data/plate_crpix_table.csv
!/data/plate_manifest.csv
/work
/logs
/tiles
*.fits
*.ldac

# Local catalogue mirrors (Gaia/PS1/USNO-B). The BUILDERS are committed under
# scripts/local_cache; the mirrors they produce are hundreds of GB.
*.parquet

# Results are committed GZIPPED only -- a 20 MB CSV re-added on every run would
# live in the pack forever. See docs/REPRODUCING.md.
results/**/*.csv
!results/**/*.csv.gz

__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*.so
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store

# Machine-specific path overrides
config.local.yaml
